{"reference":"Ezekiel 13","book":"Ezekiel","chapter":13,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Interpretive Question","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Some scholars ask whether the phrase “peace and security” in 1 Thessalonians 5:3 echoes the false promise of “Peace” in Ezekiel 13:10. The connection is disputed: it may reflect prophetic false peace, political claims, ordinary complacency, or overlapping resonances. Reading each passage within its own warning keeps this question from turning either text into predictive commentary on modern headlines.","verse_refs":["Ezekiel 13:10"],"provenance_refs":["render_path_ezekiel_013_c59a5116433616ac7321d7bd"],"confidence":"low","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}